# Project Structure

This is a Next.js 15 application with React 19 using the App Router and server components. It uses Prisma as the ORM and auth.js for user and session management

This project uses Tailwind v4 https://tailwindcss.com/blog/tailwindcss-v4 and shadcn/ui components https://ui.shadcn.com/docs

Key directories:
- `app/` - Contains the application routes using Next.js App Router
  - `app/(authenticated)/` - Routes that require authentication
  - `app/actions.ts` - Server actions for data mutations
- `components/` - Reusable UI components, including shadcn/ui
- `lib/` - Utility functions and shared code
- `prisma/` - Database schema and generated types

# Security Pattern

## Data Access Control

1. Always perform server-side validation before sending sensitive data to the client
2. Use server components to filter data before passing to client components
3. Never trust client-side state for access control decisions

Example for wishlists:

```jsx
// Server component
async function WishlistContent({ userId }) {
  const wishlists = await getWishlistsWithMembers();
  
  return (
    <div>
      {wishlists.map((wishlist) => {
        // Server-side check if user is a member
        const isMember = wishlist.members.some(m => m.id === userId);
        
        // Don't send member details to client if not a member
        if (!isMember) {
          wishlist.members = [];
        }
        
        return <WishlistCard wishlist={wishlist} isMember={isMember} />;
      })}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Cache Invalidation

When modifying data, always invalidate relevant caches:

```js
// Example from action
export const joinWishlist = async (wishlistId, pin) => {
  // Update data...
  
  // Revalidate caches
  revalidateGiftRelatedCaches();
  revalidateTag('wishlists');
  revalidateTag('wishlistsWithMembers');
  
  return { success: true, message: 'Success' };
};
```
